1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,933
The hardest published Transformer case asks a 64-gigabyte Mac to
process one hundred thousand tokens, while the explicit float32
attention matrix alone would need 18.626 tebibytes.

2
00:00:06,933 --> 00:00:12,000
Our first task was therefore not a small speed trick; it was making
the exact workload bounded and runnable.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,875
We target our own 20-core-GPU Apple M5 Pro, as allowed in the
workshop.

4
00:00:16,875 --> 00:00:19,875
All fourteen rows use float32 input and output.

5
00:00:19,875 --> 00:00:30,000
A result passes when absolute error is at most 0.002 or relative
error is at most two percent, so every optimization is checked
before it is timed.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:46,571
For rows one through thirteen, the solution combines packed
projections, safe internal half precision, PyTorch attention, frozen
fixed-shape graphs, and small fused Metal operations only where each
route won.

7
00:00:46,571 --> 00:00:54,571
Three complete organizer-default sessions measured 2.513080,
2.523037, and 2.508106 times baseline, averaging 2.514741 times.

8
00:00:54,571 --> 00:00:58,000
All 117 fresh float32 comparisons passed.

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:06,364
Row fourteen is processed one batch item at a time, never
materializing quadratic attention.

10
00:01:06,364 --> 00:01:16,519
A custom Metal 4 bridge runs Apple's MIT-licensed MLX NAX primitive
directly on PyTorch MPS storage.

11
00:01:16,519 --> 00:01:25,481
The promoted QKV kernel writes all 48 heads directly using a 32 by
512 tile.

12
00:01:25,481 --> 00:01:44,000
The attention kernel uses 256 query rows by 48 key rows, keeps
float32 softmax state, pads only query rows for alignment, and
automatically falls back if the native route is unavailable.

13
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:55,550
The current direct-head QKV change passed the explicit 8,192-token
reference, remained identical at larger lengths, and won four
balanced 100,000-token sessions by a 1.019126 geometric mean.

14
00:01:55,550 --> 00:02:01,738
The preceding safe route completed full batch 32 under the
organizer-default setting in 98.589 seconds.

15
00:02:01,738 --> 00:02:10,400
The promoted route completed three contention-controlled batch-32
runs in 54.269, 51.896, 52.003 seconds, with a 52.003-second median
and all outputs finite.

16
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:14,525
Power state was not inspected or used as a gate.

17
00:02:14,525 --> 00:02:17,000
The preceding route remains separately labelled.

18
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,333
The champion is locked by six production hashes.

19
00:02:21,333 --> 00:02:30,542
A deterministic public-safe package excludes the unlicensed
organizer attachment and private history and preserves both MIT
licences.

20
00:02:30,542 --> 00:02:40,833
Its public-safe gate passes 33 tests with one expected missing-input
skip; a checksum-matched authorized-input copy passes all 101 tests.

21
00:02:40,833 --> 00:02:43,000
Unsupported inputs fail closed.

22
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,529
We do not invent MFU, full-length reference equality, or
cross-session causal speedups.

23
00:02:46,529 --> 00:02:51,529
The result is device-specific; power state is not inspected or
controlled, and every rejected idea stays explicit.

24
00:02:51,529 --> 00:02:58,000
The contribution is a measured Apple-native Transformer path, a
runnable giant row, and an evidence trail that makes every
performance claim auditable.
